            "The field test does not produce an automatic verdict. It organizes questions for negotiators, counsel, technical experts, and political decision-makers. A proposal may be acceptable despite residual risks if those risks are understood, lawfully authorized, and monitored. An arrangement may be rejected not because it lacks perfect symmetry, but because its accountability and safeguards are insufficient for the consequences it can impose.",
