            "Comparing Versailles with the ECSC is tempting because the cases appear to contrast punishment with integration. Yet they differ in time, participants, purpose, international environment, and the condition of the states involved. A counterfactual must account for those differences rather than assume that the post-1945 arrangement could simply have been inserted into the Paris peace negotiations of 1919.",
