            "The post-1945 European settlement cannot be explained by the ECSC in isolation. Western European reconstruction involved national policies, the Marshall Plan, American security commitments, the formation of NATO, changing relations with West Germany, and the gradual creation of other European institutions. The Cold War shaped both the perceived threat environment and the political incentives for cooperation. A serious account includes these factors rather than presenting coal and steel pooling as a self-sufficient peace machine.",
