            "The Fiduciary Standard is an internal ethical and strategic rule for Chancellery operators. It asks a negotiator to consider whether the proposed bargain would foreseeably undermine the other party's ability to sustain basic institutions and whether the resulting instability would also threaten the negotiating state's interests. It is not, without an applicable legal source, a general doctrine that one sovereign owes a private-law fiduciary duty to another. Its force within the curriculum comes from the governing Chancellery framework, and its application should be transparent about that status.",
