            "After implementation begins, the record can be updated with observed effects, changes in assumptions, and review decisions. The original should remain intact so that later readers can distinguish what was known at signature from what was learned afterward. This protects institutional memory without suggesting that later evidence automatically changes the legal meaning of the agreement.",
